awk
----
-awk is used for data extraction and reporting. 
-It works on a line-by-line basis.
-More powrfull than cut command.

Prints all lines.
-----------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk '{print}' data.txt
java|2000|language
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Prints the first field. Default delimiter is space.
---------------------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk -F '|' '{print $1}' data.txt
java
mysql
oracle
python
django

Prints the first and second field.
----------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk -F '|' '{print $1,$2}' data.txt
java 2000
mysql 5000
oracle 4000
python 3000
django 3000

In cut(| show )
--------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cut -d '|' -f 1-2 data.txt
java|2000
mysql|5000
oracle|4000
python|3000
django|3000

-Awk use mostly

Prints lines containing "language"
-----------------------------------
create a file

[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat > data2.txt
java|2000|language
mysql|4000|database
python|3000|language
django|3000|language

[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk '/language/{print}' data2.txt
java|2000|language
python|3000|language
django|3000|language

 Prints first field of lines containing "language"
-------------------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk -F '|' '/language/{print $1}' data2.txt
java
python
django

Print course name contain language
------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk -F '|' '/language/{print $1}' data2.txt
java
python

Print only specific row eg.=2(NR==2)
------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk 'NR==2 {print}' data.txt
mysql|5000|database

Print 2nd row with 2nd column
------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk -F '|' 'NR==2 {print $2}' data.txt
5000

Print all rows but except 2 row(NR!=2)
---------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk "NR!=2 {print}" data.txt
java|2000|language
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Display courses where course fee is more than 3000
--------------------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk -F '|' '$2>3000 {print}' data.txt
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database

-This type of questions not solve in cut command.

Display courses where course fee is more than 2000 and course type is language
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk -F '|' '$2>2000 && $3=="language" {print}' data.txt
django|3000|language

    OR
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk -F '|' '$2>2000 && /language/ {print}' data.txt
django|3000|language





